mpi4pyscf 0.4.0
---------------
Bind to pyscf>=2.5, mpi4py>=4.0, Python>=3.13  (tested with pyscf-2.13.0,
mpi4py-4.1.2, Open MPI 4.1.6, Python 3.13, numpy 2.5)
* Bugfix
  - Deadlock on all worker ranks at the end of mpi.work_share_partition (used
    by CCSD(T)) on Python>=3.3.  The worker event loop runs inside the import
    of mpi4pyscf, and a helper thread unpickling mpi.Message blocked forever
    on the package's import lock.
  - NameError in CCSD(T) kernel and in the full-vvvv CCSD path
    (process_clock/perf_counter), undefined _mo_without_core, and a typo in
    CCSD.gather_amplitudes
  - MP2 on workers failed with PySCF>=2.x (no _scf object on workers)
  - lib.diis.restore referenced an undefined name; numpy.linalg.linalg no
    longer exists in numpy 2
* Changed
  - Removed the distutils-based version check (distutils is gone in Python
    3.12). pyscf>=2.5 is now required
  - Warn at startup if the MPI library does not provide MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE
  - Tests compare to serial PySCF instead of hardcoded energies; added tests
    for CCSD/CCSD(T) and the mpi4pyscf.tools.mpi communication helpers
* Known issues
  - mpi4pyscf.pbc (PBC density fitting) is not compatible with pyscf>=2.x

